+## Current consumer and evidence inventory
+
+The current reusable workflow's `review` job exposes
+`steps.codex.outputs.final-message` as `final_message` in
+[architecture-gate.yml](../../.github/workflows/architecture-gate.yml#L208).
+The consumer copy does the same in
+[architecture-gate-consumer.yml](../../.github/workflows/architecture-gate-consumer.yml#L174).
+The Action also receives the configured output schema. Current downstream
+deterministic checks are consumer rules and Authority Set checks; there is no
+separate current “consumer-schema” handoff step. A proposed self-only issuer
+would independently validate the prepared CI decision with
+`validatePreparedCiDecision` before issuing. The value is then used in these
+distinct paths:
+
+- **Main review job:** `final_message` is sent to decision-kind, configured
+  consumer-rule and complete-Authority-Set checks. The review job also records
+  reviewed SHA and authority provenance. The upstream Action uses the selected
+  output schema; a proposed issuer would independently validate the prepared
+  CI decision. Exact original bytes and canonical decision digest are distinct
+  values; neither is reusable acceptance authority by itself.
+- **BLOCK record:** the protected `block-review-record` job consumes the
+  `final_message` output and authority provenance to create the versioned
+  exact-byte ReviewRecord and its attestation. See
+  [workflow lines 503–515](../../.github/workflows/architecture-gate.yml#L503).
+- **OWNER_ADDITION:** the protected addition preparation consumes
+  `ORDINARY_DECISION` and provenance, then uses the complete decision and
+  policy inputs to produce its procedure and eligibility request. See
+  [workflow lines 632–644](../../.github/workflows/architecture-gate.yml#L632).
+- **OWNER_AMENDMENT:** the owner-decision trigger-record path consumes exact
+  decision bytes and provenance for the trigger ReviewRecord and AmendmentRecord;
+  see [workflow lines 719–730](../../.github/workflows/architecture-gate.yml#L719).
+- **Report:** the protected report job consumes the ordinary decision,
+  review result, reviewed revision and provenance to classify, render, and
+  digest the full report. Its same-run conclusion/status is consumed by accept;
+  see [report inputs](../../.github/workflows/architecture-gate.yml#L1100).
+- **Accept:** the current enforced and procedural accept commands consume
+  `needs.review.result` and the same-run `needs.report.outputs.conclusion`,
+  plus selected OWNER_ADDITION result/eligibility where applicable; see
+  [acceptance inputs](../../.github/workflows/architecture-gate.yml#L1192).
+
+The current acceptance contract describes the decision digest and reviewed SHA
+as report metadata rather than a standalone independently accepted artifact
+([architecture.md, current acceptance](../architecture.md#current-acceptance-mechanism)).
+Existing BLOCK, OWNER_ADDITION, and OWNER_AMENDMENT records have their own
+trigger-specific exact-byte and provenance rules. A proposed PASS handoff must
+not be mistaken for or silently substituted into those records.
+
+## Proposed direction for canonical owner choice
+
+A candidate design for owner consideration is a **self-repository only,
+protected, same-run semantic result** for the ordinary Codex `PASS` on
+`flair-agency/architecture-gatekeeper` MAIN. It applies only to the current
+self profile with its complete six-member protected Authority Set. Generic
+reusable consumers and their v1, v5, and governance paths retain their existing
+behavior. In this design only the protected self review job could issue a
+fixed result after deterministic checks confirm the exact protected self
+policy and selector, selected protected runtime source revision, and complete
+six-authority selection, then independently validate the prepared CI decision
+with the full schema and every consumer rule. Proposed version 1 is a fixed
+record with kind `ordinary-self-pass`, conclusion `PASS`, exact original
+decision byte SHA-256 and current canonical decision digest, protected
+policy/schema/consumer-rule digests, complete Authority Set digest,
+repository/PR/base/head/reviewed revision, caller and reusable workflow
+ref/SHA, run/attempt, protected producer job identity, verified reporter
+identity, and a fresh nonce. Fixed same-run job outputs carry the result;
+candidate content and reviewer output cannot select its version or producer.
+Serialization and runtime function names are implementation details after
+authorization. The protected prior policy selects this route explicitly; a
+missing output or service failure cannot dynamically enable it as fallback.
+This is same-run metadata, not portable evidence. The proposed PASS payload's
+raw reviewer bytes remain job-local. Existing non-PASS trigger-specific paths
+retain their original cross-job decision transport and exact-byte requirements. The
+handoff covers PASS only; it does not reinterpret
+`BLOCK`, `OWNER_DECISION`, OWNER_ADDITION, OWNER_AMENDMENT, or governance output.
+
+A protected self reporter and the self accept consumer would verify the same
+immutable workflow, run, attempt, job, revision and nonce bindings. The
+reporter retains its current isolated `pull-requests: write` responsibility;
+it may receive `actions: read` if selected and needed for verification. That
+job-token permission grants repository-wide Actions read access; the protected
+runtime must restrict its requests to this exact run, attempt and selected job.
+No additional review PR-write, OIDC,
+or secret capability is proposed. For human rendering, the reporter may parse
+the returned masked display projection, but must never treat it as semantic
+evidence or exact original bytes. The projection is the original JSON passed
+through the runner's existing masking. Workflow command processing is disabled
+while emitting it. There is no unmasked raw-artifact or encoded log channel.
+Raw private PASS bytes remain in the review job; existing exact trigger evidence
+for non-PASS decisions retains its original transport and validation.
+Missing, truncated, malformed, stale or mismatched fixed outputs or report
+inputs fail closed; no artifact retrieval is proposed for this PASS route.
+
+This choice would introduce a semantic-result issuer and consumer trust
+relationship that the selected Authority Set does not currently choose. An
+owner must first record the canonical decision and its exact scope in the
+appropriate authority member. This proposal is not that amendment and cannot
+be cited as authority.
+
+Suggested canonical owner question: **Does the owner authorize this exact
+self-only version-1 ordinary Codex PASS result and same-run fixed-output,
+protected reporter and accept trust path on MAIN, with the fields and
+permission bounds specified above; generic reusable consumers and their
+v1/v5/governance paths unchanged; original bytes kept job-local; masked log
+projection used only for rendering; and BLOCK/OWNER_DECISION/OWNER_ADDITION/
+OWNER_AMENDMENT retaining their existing exact-byte paths?** This is one
+bounded trust/scope choice; serialization and function names remain ordinary
+implementation decisions. Until it is canonically recorded, current fail-closed
+behavior stands: suppression leaves the result incomplete. This proposal
+claims only partial #329 progress and does not promote the publicly reported
+raw PASS for PR #522 to protected acceptance.
+
+At current source baseline `bb7c6078766e2d63cbcaf91e8eab72a7bd46a83f`, an
+initial native conceptual review independently returned a validated
+`OWNER_DECISION` for all six selected authorities. It is local feedback only:
+it is neither CI acceptance nor owner authorization and does not establish a
+protected implementation. That concept assumed no additional permissions;
+`actions: read` remains an explicit proposed capability for owner selection,
+not an already-reviewed implementation. No implementation or live fix exists
+in this proposal; it records no rerun of PR #522, Gemini activation, or
+acceptance waiver.
+
+## Review and rollout checks if an owner selects this direction
+
+Before implementation, obtain the canonical owner decision, then review the
+producer, reporter, report and accept trust boundaries together. The focused
+negative verification should cover:
+
+| Fixture or mutation | Required outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| Invalid decision schema, consumer rule, authority digest, omitted/extra/duplicate authority member | No semantic result; accept fails |
+| Failed, cancelled, skipped or incomplete review | No semantic result; accept fails |
+| Safe secret-free dummy marker in a generated test response | Verify output-suppression behavior without probing secrets; no reliance on masked text |
+| Wrong run, attempt, workflow/job identity, repository, policy or reviewed SHA; replayed context | Reporter/accept reject the binding |
+| Missing, malformed, truncated, oversized or suppressed fixed output/report data | Fail closed; no alternate log parser or fallback |
+| Newline or command-like text in diagnostic material | Remains inert display data; cannot issue workflow commands |
+| Missing/suppressed result or report conclusion | Accept fails closed |
+| Non-PASS outcomes including BLOCK and OWNER_DECISION; selected governance procedure absent or failed | Preserve current governance behavior; never become ordinary PASS |
+
+Any eventual rollout is staged: after owner choice, review the implementation;
+adopt it through protected MAIN governance; then run fresh current-head CI and
+inspect exact workflow/run/attempt evidence. Do not infer or borrow the inactive
+Gemini selection or the Issue #210 self-only reporter as authorization for
+this consumer. No result here changes #525's inactive registration or
+authorizes acceptance of PR #522.
+
